Z","closed_at":"2025-07-24T19:00:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in Godot 4.4.1 stable to 4.5 beta 3\n\n### System information\n\nEnvironment: Godot Version: 4.4.1 and 4.5 beta 3 (official) , Device: Redmi Note 10 , OS: Android 11 , Architecture: arm64-v8a\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the Android version of the Godot Editor (tested in versions 4.4.1 and 4.5 beta 3), there is a persistent editor bug:\n\nWhen switching between open scenes using the scene tabs at the top of the editor, the 2D/3D view correctly updates to the selected scene, but the script editor does not update to match the new scene.\n\nThe previously open script remains active, requiring manual navigation to the corresponding script of the newly selected scene.\n\nExpected Behaviour: (as in windows version)\nWhen switching scenes using the top scene tabs:\n\nThe editor should also switch the visible script in the script panel to match the root node's attached script of the newly active scene (or open the first available script in that scene if none is attached to the root).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\nOpen Godot 4.4.1 or 4.5 beta 3 on Android.\n\nOpen two or more scenes (e.g., SceneA.tscn and SceneB.tscn).\n\nTap the tab to switch from one scene to another.\n\nObserve that the 2D/3D viewport changes correctly, but the script panel still shows the previous script.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"http